analysis:
Examined the Autopilot placement/adoption, transition watchdog and wire-schema changes.

Adoption: ProviderLoop+AutopilotPlacement.swift:34-38 lets an adopted inventory model keep serving after its lease ends. Withdrawal is now skipped for valid adoptions (ProviderLoop+AutopilotInventory.swift:15). The adoption basis (lines 22-26) still requires all of the following:
- not shutting down;
- saved consent;
- operator selection (autopilotSettings.allows);
- a resident slot;
- not retiring;
- no failed self-test;
- a non-empty liveModelHashes entry.

reconcileAutopilotPlacements (78-86) drops adoptions whose basis has ended and then re-runs withdrawal. Adoption therefore does not appear to widen serving beyond verified, operator-selected builds (T-012, T-027 weight-hash posture unchanged). Integration should confirm that reconcile runs on every basis change, as the comment claims: snapshot publication and unload. It should also check that autopilotServesModel is the gate used at request admission.

Holds: holds (62-70) only affect eviction and idle unload of advertised, verified models. Their only effect is local availability and memory.

Uncertainty: the doc says holdSeconds is limited to 0...86400 (ModelAutopilot.swift:160). However, recordAutopilotPlacement line 69 computes Int64(seconds) * 1_000 with a trapping multiply, and line 68 uses .seconds(seconds), with no visible clamp. The coordinator is trusted, so this is not a finding. Integration should still verify that command acceptance or decoding validates the hold_seconds range. Otherwise an out-of-range value could crash the provider process.

Watchdog: TransitionWatchdog.swift and ProviderLoop+TransitionWatchdog.swift only take three actions, and never clear fences:
- cancel the owned autopilot task;
- set the startupPreload stop flag;
- answer a stalled preload as failed (line 96).

Integration should check that a late preload result is suppressed after finishPreloadTask, as the comment claims. It should also check that cancelling an autopilot task mid-publication leaves pendingAdvertise and the reserve consistent; Inventory 72-86 handles the throw path.

Logs and new snapshot fields (adopted_models, held_models, busy_reasons, transition_stalls; decoding in ModelAutopilotSnapshot+Decoding.swift 33-56) expose only model IDs, command IDs and timings to the trusted coordinator. No prompt data (A-001) or keys are exposed.

No change was found to encryption, attestation, App Attest authorization (TB-011) or cache (T-041) paths.
